information. The inverse velocity and associated mass are calculated from,

\[\frac{1}{\beta}=\frac{c\Delta t}{s} \tag{4.2}\]

\[M^{2}=p^{2}\Big{(}\big{(}\frac{1}{\beta}\big{)}^{2}-1\Big{)} \tag{4.3}\]

where p = momentum,

\(\Delta t\) = flight time,

s = total path length,

c = velocity of light.

The PID capabilities of the STAR detector using TOF are shown in Fig. 4.8. From the above

Figure 4.8: Momentum dependence of the particle identification capabilities of a TOF system with a time resolution of 100 ps [102].

