Here, \(f_{n}^{obs}\) is \(n\)-th order efficiency uncorrected factorial moment and \(f_{n}^{inc}\) is \(n\)-th order efficiency corrected factorial moment. We denote all observed (or efficiency uncorrected) quantities in a small alphabet (like \(f_{n}^{obs}\) as \(f_{n}\)) and all incident or efficiency corrected observables in capital alphabet (like \(f_{n}^{inc}\) as \(F_{n}\)).

